        "body": "<!-- proofline:finding-series=01a202cc-b228-7589-938f-c1270a0c8ac1 -->\n**Warning** \u00b7 Concurrent startups can abort a console command during upgrade\n\nTwo startups can both read `user_version` as 1 before either commits, so the second can try to drop `legacy_format` after the first removed it.\n\nThe second invocation raises `OperationalError` before dispatching its command. Even a single-row `schedule` waits for rewrite I/O proportional to the table size.\n\nAcquire a write transaction before reading `user_version` and apply migrations without releasing that transaction.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details</summary>\n\nBefore this change, a version-1 database skipped all migration writes. Execute migration statements without `executescript` if it would implicitly commit the transaction holding the write lock.\n\n</details>\n\n[View finding in Proofline](https://proofline.sh/orgs/by-id/01a202a0-cd61-7684-99bc-53c775b0de50/reviews/01a202cb-5979-770c-a409-14a10c84aeeb/findings/01a202cc-b22c-7411-8ca1-426987d49ecc)\n\nAlso at:\n- [`migrations/001_initial.sql`](https://github.com/Pratik8445/bench-run-coderabbit/blob/420baea889887b127f1c87d99f728e40f7664996/migrations/001_initial.sql#L1-L8) lines 1 to 8\n- [`reports.py`](https://github.com/Pratik8445/bench-run-coderabbit/blob/420baea889887b127f1c87d99f728e40f7664996/reports.py#L13-L29) lines 13 to 29",
